The best way is to get a "safe" count of the seconds like this:

PROC SafeSex&:
    LOCAL t1&,t2&

    DO
        t1&=t2&
        t2&=DATETOSECS(YEAR,MONTH,DAY,HOUR,MINUTE,SECOND)
    UNTIL t1&=t2&

    RETURN t1&
ENDP

Note that the procedure is designed this way in order to ensure that a 
minimum of *two* identical samples of the time have taken place. This 
avoids the slim chance that the minutes or hours etc. have clocked over 
*during* the sampling of the time.

Regards,
Jezar.

  

